dilution":80.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.02165,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":14.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Steven Madden, Ltd. designs, sources, and markets fashion-forward branded and private label footwear, accessories, and apparel in the United States and internationally. It operates through Wholesale Footwear, Wholesale Accessories/Apparel, Direct-to- Consumer, and Licensing segments. The company designs, sources, and markets various products, including dress shoes, boots, booties, fashion sneakers, sandals, and casual shoes; and handbags, apparel, small leather goods, belts, soft accessories, fashion scarves, wraps, gifting, and other accessories. It also engages in the sale of footwear, handbags, apparel, and other accessories. In addition, the company is involved in the licensing of the Steve Madden, Kurt Geiger, and Betsey Johnson trademarks for the sale of select apparel, accessory, home categories, and other non-core products. It sells its products under the Steve Madden, Kurt Geiger London, Dolce Vita, Betsey Johnson, Blondo, Carvela, Anthony Thomas Melillo (ATM), and Anne Klein brands. The company distributes its products in the wholesale channel through department stores, mass merchants, off-price retailers, shoe chains, online retailers, national chains, specialty retailers, independent stores, and clubs, as well as through direct-to-consumer channel, which includes company-operated retail stores and e-commerce websites. It markets its products through email, social media, influencer partnerships, print, experiential events, and public relations. The company was incorporated in 1990 and is headquartered in Long Island City, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Edward R. Rosenfeld | Chairman & CEO | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $603K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $28K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Steven Madden, Ltd. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.9B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 29% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 19-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 38%.","The business throws off $120M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.31\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 6.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 41% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.41082411731784985},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2264142.48},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Steven Madden Ltd (SHOO) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Revenue Jumps 16% as EPS Surges ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/steven-madden-ltd-shoo-q3-010945349.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794013785.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Steven Madden (SHOO) Reports Q3 Earnings: What Key Metrics Have to Say","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025930/steven-madden-shoo-reports-q3-earnings-what-key-metrics-have-to-say?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-3025930","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793998802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"SHOO Q3 Earnings Beat on Wholesale Strength, 2026 Outlook Raised","source":"zacks.com","link"